# Working with Montra

A Montra ticket is an implementation spec, written from what the person said and did on
screen. Start from `list_documents` or `get_document`.

## Treat the connection as read only

The tickets are the person's spec. Report progress in conversation, not by editing
Montra.

- Do not create, update, or delete documents or tickets unless the user explicitly asks
  for that change in the current conversation.
- Never mark a ticket implemented, done, or complete by rewriting its title, summary, or
  body. There is no ticket status to set, and an unrequested edit overwrites what the
  person wrote.
- `link_ticket_issue` is the exception. When the user asks you to create a Linear or
  Notion issue from a ticket, recording that link is part of the export, so it needs no
  separate ask.

## Getting context

- A ticket's screenshots usually carry the detail the text leaves implicit. Look at them
  before deciding scope.
- The transcript is worth reading when the wording of a ticket is ambiguous.
- When the user pastes a Montra share link, resolve it with the share link tool instead
  of fetching the web page.
